So if you want the highest score, make sure you have all of
the items you need to ascend, then fill up on high point
value items until you are just barely not burdened.  Then as
you progress from level to level ditch the items you will no
longer need (digging after air and so on) that don't give
points.

You'll want to look up point value against weight if you want
to maximize score.  The highest point to weight ratio items
are the unique ones.  Then it depends on exactly which item
whether it has a better point to weight ratio than a dilithium
crystal.  Then gems by value.  It turns out gold is dead last
in this system of measuring the point to weight ratio.

Something to consider once you've ascended once -
Ascending at all beats any non-ascension score even if the
point score is lower.  Once you can ascend occasionally
the skill comparison starts to be percentage of games
ascended and lowest score at ascension.  That's the
opposite of scoring desire before ascending.  Before
ascending getting higher scores means you are progressing
in some sense.  After ascending getting higher scores
means putting time into activities other than ascending.
Strange how it reverses meaning like that and is not a
good measurement of skill in either case.


